\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. Come ye sinners, poor and wretched,
\par Weak and wounded, sick and sore;
\par Jesus ready stands to save you,
\par Full of pity, joined with power:
\par He is able,
\par He is willing; doubt no more.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. Come, ye needy, come, and welcome;
\par God's free bounty glorify;
\par True belief and true repentance,
\par Every grace that brings us nigh,
\par Without money
\par Come to Jesus Christ and buy.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. Come, ye weary, heavy-laden,
\par Bruised and broken by the fall;
\par If you tarry till you're better,
\par You will never come at all:
\par Not the righteous-
\par Sinners Jesus came to call.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. Let not conscience make you linger,
\par Nor of fitness fondly dream;
\par All the fitness He requireth
\par Is to feel your need of Him:
\par This He gives you;
\par 'Tis the Spirit's rising beam.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 5\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 5. Lo! the incarnate God, ascended,
\par Pleads the merit of His blood;
\par venture on Him, venture wholly;
\par Let no other trust intrude:
\par None but Jesus
\par Can do helpless sinners good.\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b 
\par }

